# Credentials for the tools the agent runs, as environment variables of the container.
# Copy to .env for Docker Compose; on Kubernetes they go in the elseagent-env Secret.
#
# All optional: they just sign the tools in non-interactively. You can also open a shell in the
# container (docker compose exec elseagent bash) and sign in by hand (gh auth login…); logins
# saved in the home directory persist in the volume. Uncomment what you use.

# GitHub: gh, and git over HTTPS for github.com
# GH_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# Cloudflare: wrangler
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=...
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=...

# Kubernetes: kubectl and helm (mount the file too)
# KUBECONFIG=/home/elseagent/.kube/config

# Postgres: psql (standard libpq variables)
# PGHOST=...
# PGPORT=5432
# PGUSER=...
# PGPASSWORD=...
# PGDATABASE=...

# MySQL / MariaDB: mariadb
# MYSQL_HOST=...
# MYSQL_PWD=...

# sops: the age key that decrypts the repositories' encrypted files
# SOPS_AGE_KEY=AGE-SECRET-KEY-...
